    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1571">

                <pb facs="1245" n="1235" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1235"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Olive, William M.: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-18T18:00:00+08:00">June [<hi
                                rendition="#italic">July</hi>] 18, 1949—6 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 18—9:47 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1548. Embassy has delayed making further protest to local Communist authorities
                    over treatment Vice Consul Olive (Deptel 1382, July 11 to Shanghai) to avoid
                    conflict with current negotiations Mr. and Mrs. Olive’s exit from China. Olive
                    is in Nanking, his exit from <pb facs="1246" n="1236" xml:id="pg1236"/> China
                    hangs in balance along with other members of Ambassador’s party awaiting exit
                    permits and Embassy is loath to take any action at this time which might
                    exacerbate already strained situation locally and thus prejudice Olive’s chance
                    departing China with Ambassador. If Department concurs we prefer make protest
                    envisaged in Department telegram under reference after Olive has left for US or
                    after negotiations his exit have ended in failure.<anchor n="21"
                        xml:id="d1571-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent Department 1548, repeated Shanghai 865, Dept pass Peiping 28.</p>
                <closer>[<signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1571-f1" n="21" xml:id="d1571-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 846, July 19, 5 p. m., Department informed the Ambassador that it
                    concurred in this procedure.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
